## Summary

I implemented **`page:analytics/Timeline`** as a native SwiftUI/HIG page at full web parity, adaptive across macOS + iOS, and verified it with real build/lint/test gates.

**Delivered (`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Analytics/`):**
- `TimelineModels.swift`, `TimelineFormat.swift` — SI value types + display-boundary formatters
- `TimelinePageModel.swift` + `.Sample.swift` — `@Observable` model with a `TimelineDataSource` seam (`loadVehicles` ← the named `useVehicles` hook, plus transitions + summary), phase machine, and all derivations (indexed rows, UTC daily-breakdown bins, proportional distribution, the four metrics)
- `TimelinePage.swift` + `.Sections.swift` + `.Charts.swift` — adaptive view: 4 metric cards, state-distribution bar + legend, daily-breakdown **stacked Swift Charts BarChart**, transitions `TSDataTable`, loading/empty/error/success states
- `TimelineRouteRegistration.swift` + a new `.timeline` `AppRoute` case, composed into `TeslaSyncApp`
- `TimelinePageModelTests.swift` (XCTest), +23 verbatim `timeline.*` strings in `Localizable.xcstrings`, `apple-ledger.json` +2 rows (apple-macos + apple-ios, 35/35)

